                <pb facs="0174" n="160" xml:id="pg160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">874.00/10–2446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Representative in
                        Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Barnes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-10-24T19:00:00-05:00">October 24, 1946—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>349. Deptel 5412 to Paris rptd Sofia 322. For your info, in reply Brit Emb <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> Oct 9 Dept informed Brit Oct 23 that
                    in absence effective implementation Moscow Declaration and in light recent
                    measures taken by Bulg Govt re forthcoming elections US Govt extremely reluctant
                    extend recognition at present. US Govt appreciates considerations prompting Brit
                    Govt suggest recognition at time peace treaty signed but considers recognition
                    undesirable unless situation Bulgaria is altered by developments in meantime.
                    Despite whatever statement of technical motives for recognition might accompany
                    recognition, such recognition would probably be exploited in certain circles as
                    contradiction position and principles US and UK have been endeavoring uphold in
                    Balkans. US Govt is considering various alternatives whereby peace treaty could
                    be brought into effect without formal recognition present Bulg Govt. No final
                    decision yet reached but as some time will elapse before agreement achieved on
                    final treaty draft US Govt prefers postpone determination its course but will
                    consult Brit when final draft imminent. US shares Brit opposition to withdrawal
                    US UK Mil Missions from ACC at present.</p>
                <p>Sent Sofia 349 rptd London 7352.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
